1
00:00:00,380 --> 00:00:04,575
Welcome to Wind Desk, a historical wind intelligence workbench
for electricity

2
00:00:04,595 --> 00:00:08,662
procurement teams. This is a walkthrough of the real
application and

3
00:00:08,682 --> 00:00:13,137
its implementation. We will replay a January purchase decision,
quantify

4
00:00:13,157 --> 00:00:17,169
forecast error, and follow the data from Elexon through Python
and Postgres

5
00:00:17,189 --> 00:00:18,351
to the React dashboard.

6
00:00:19,814 --> 00:00:23,536
A utility needs to buy electricity before the delivery day,
while wind

7
00:00:23,556 --> 00:00:27,738
generation depends on weather. The analyst needs the forecast
available

8
00:00:27,758 --> 00:00:31,689
at the decision deadline, together with a defensible view of
its uncertainty.

9
00:00:32,233 --> 00:00:36,264
Looking only at the latest number today cannot reconstruct what
was known

10
00:00:36,284 --> 00:00:37,601
at an earlier cutoff.

11
00:00:39,047 --> 00:00:41,261
Wind Desk separates those two questions.

12
00:00:41,773 --> 00:00:44,633
Decision outlook contains eligible forecasts only.

13
00:00:45,178 --> 00:00:48,241
Accuracy compares them with later reported generation.

14
00:00:48,795 --> 00:00:52,369
Both retain the selected release, cutoff and source references.

15
00:00:52,904 --> 00:00:55,822
This pilot uses only Elexon national wind data.

16
00:00:56,328 --> 00:00:59,626
It does not infer the amount a particular utility should buy
without

17
00:00:59,646 --> 00:01:01,377
demand and existing positions.

18
00:01:02,814 --> 00:01:04,940
Here is the actual deployed Decision view.

19
00:01:05,511 --> 00:01:07,324
January thirty-first at nine a.m.

20
00:01:07,344 --> 00:01:09,509
concerns delivery on February first.

21
00:01:10,054 --> 00:01:12,904
All twenty-four native forecast targets are available.

22
00:01:13,420 --> 00:01:16,618
The midnight forecast is ten thousand and ninety-nine
megawatts.

23
00:01:17,143 --> 00:01:20,595
Its selected issue is seven thirty a.m., so the age at the

24
00:01:20,615 --> 00:01:22,819
cutoff is one hour and thirty minutes.

25
00:01:24,280 --> 00:01:26,378
Now the cutoff changes to nine forty-five.

26
00:01:26,891 --> 00:01:30,498
The unapplied warning keeps the current analysis and download
from being

27
00:01:30,518 --> 00:01:35,278
confused with an edit. After Apply, the nine thirty issue
becomes eligible.

28
00:01:35,803 --> 00:01:38,937
The midnight forecast becomes ten thousand four hundred and
seventy-four

29
00:01:38,957 --> 00:01:41,643
megawatts, and its age becomes fifteen minutes.

30
00:01:42,178 --> 00:01:45,723
The chart and publication ledger expose exact target values.

31
00:01:47,147 --> 00:01:50,431
Accuracy evaluates the full January range at this cutoff.

32
00:01:50,973 --> 00:01:53,679
All seven hundred and forty-four native targets pair.

33
00:01:54,214 --> 00:01:57,772
Mean absolute error is about one thousand nine hundred and
ninety-six

34
00:01:57,792 --> 00:02:01,804
megawatts. Root mean square error is about two thousand four
hundred

35
00:02:01,824 --> 00:02:05,735
and ninety-nine. Positive bias shows average overforecasting.

36
00:02:06,289 --> 00:02:10,291
P ninety absolute error is a historical statistic, not a
guaranteed future

37
00:02:10,311 --> 00:02:10,808
buffer.

38
00:02:12,247 --> 00:02:14,895
Selecting a decision day narrows the historical review.

39
00:02:15,446 --> 00:02:19,174
The chart, coverage, error summary and CSV follow that
selection.

40
00:02:19,728 --> 00:02:23,663
The export retains all actual half-hours and explicitly marks
native

41
00:02:23,683 --> 00:02:27,768
comparison targets. A saved view keeps its release when
reopened.

42
00:02:28,332 --> 00:02:32,581
Missing values remain gaps with reasons, rather than becoming
zero generation.

43
00:02:34,047 --> 00:02:37,904
Data and methodology shows nineteen thousand eight hundred and
fifty-six

44
00:02:37,924 --> 00:02:41,348
forecast versions and one thousand four hundred and eighty-
eight actual

45
00:02:41,368 --> 00:02:45,710
observations. Source rows open response references and
checksums.

46
00:02:46,235 --> 00:02:50,098
The analysis dialog exposes the full context and release
identities.

47
00:02:50,624 --> 00:02:53,748
These references let a reviewer trace a visible figure back to
the

48
00:02:53,768 --> 00:02:55,152
accepted source evidence.

49
00:02:56,580 --> 00:03:00,225
For every delivery target, the selector first restricts
publications

50
00:03:00,245 --> 00:03:02,035
to those at or before the cutoff.

51
00:03:02,567 --> 00:03:06,025
It chooses the latest eligible key, and only then checks
quality.

52
00:03:06,560 --> 00:03:10,388
A null or conflicting latest issue stays invalid; it does not
silently

53
00:03:10,408 --> 00:03:12,496
fall back to an older valid forecast.

54
00:03:13,032 --> 00:03:15,448
Decision analysis does not load actuals.

55
00:03:16,880 --> 00:03:18,814
Errors are forecast minus actual.

56
00:03:19,317 --> 00:03:23,393
The metrics module calculates mean absolute error, root mean
square error,

57
00:03:23,542 --> 00:03:26,498
signed bias and an interpolated ninetieth percentile.

58
00:03:27,004 --> 00:03:29,411
With no valid pairs, metrics are null.

59
00:03:29,937 --> 00:03:33,703
Hourly forecast targets match actuals at equal source
timestamps.

60
00:03:34,248 --> 00:03:38,395
The intervening actual half-hours remain in exports; forecasts
are not

61
00:03:38,415 --> 00:03:40,242
invented between hourly targets.

62
00:03:41,680 --> 00:03:45,698
The browser reaches the Vercel HTTPS endpoint and project
firewall.

63
00:03:46,201 --> 00:03:50,502
FastAPI serves both the compiled React assets and read APIs
from that

64
00:03:50,522 --> 00:03:54,900
origin. Analysis services use bounded caches and a restricted
database

65
00:03:54,920 --> 00:03:58,127
reader. Pure domain functions calculate the result.

66
00:03:58,681 --> 00:04:02,597
The response includes an analysis identity and a matching
guarded C S

67
00:04:02,617 --> 00:04:03,345
V download.

68
00:04:04,814 --> 00:04:06,719
Ingestion is separate from browsing.

69
00:04:07,270 --> 00:04:11,561
The operator command fetches or replays original Elexon
responses, validates

70
00:04:11,581 --> 00:04:13,988
them, and publishes an accepted release.

71
00:04:14,523 --> 00:04:18,863
Database tables retain raw batches, forecast and actual
versions, immutable

72
00:04:18,883 --> 00:04:20,875
membership, and an active-release pointer.

73
00:04:21,419 --> 00:04:24,221
A failed candidate does not replace accepted data.

74
00:04:24,737 --> 00:04:27,819
The web function receives only the restricted reader
credential.

75
00:04:29,247 --> 00:04:32,670
When the analyst edits a date or cutoff, React keeps the draft

76
00:04:32,690 --> 00:04:34,316
distinct from the applied result.

77
00:04:34,857 --> 00:04:38,325
Applying a valid selection updates the URL and query key.

78
00:04:38,879 --> 00:04:42,785
Fetch sends the selected date, local cutoff and release to the
decision-view

79
00:04:42,805 --> 00:04:47,607
endpoint. FastAPI rejects invalid or duplicate filters before
analysis

80
00:04:47,627 --> 00:04:48,172
begins.

81
00:04:49,614 --> 00:04:51,538
React builds the three analyst views.

82
00:04:52,089 --> 00:04:56,029
TypeScript and runtime response validation help catch contract
mismatches.

83
00:04:56,565 --> 00:04:59,116
Vite provides development and production builds.

84
00:04:59,651 --> 00:05:03,707
TanStack Query manages filter-specific requests, cancellation
and refresh.

85
00:05:04,242 --> 00:05:08,476
Native SVG charts and HTML dialogs keep exact values and

86
00:05:08,496 --> 00:05:12,170
references keyboard-accessible, with responsive layouts and
reduced-motion

87
00:05:12,190 --> 00:05:12,773
support.

88
00:05:14,214 --> 00:05:18,457
FastAPI exposes typed read routes, while Pydantic validates
filters and

89
00:05:18,477 --> 00:05:22,861
response contracts. Python domain functions contain selection
and metric

90
00:05:22,881 --> 00:05:27,568
rules independently of HTTP. SQLAlchemy and Psycopg connect to
Postgres

91
00:05:27,588 --> 00:05:29,918
using bound parameters and a small pool.

92
00:05:30,414 --> 00:05:34,320
Alembic versions the schema. This separation makes the business
rules

93
00:05:34,340 --> 00:05:35,570
independently testable.

94
00:05:36,980 --> 00:05:39,647
Elexon is the only analytical data integration.

95
00:05:40,199 --> 00:05:42,721
Docker Compose reproduces the application locally.

96
00:05:43,266 --> 00:05:46,010
GitHub Actions runs quality and container checks.

97
00:05:46,545 --> 00:05:50,119
Vercel hosts the web application, and Neon hosts Postgres.

98
00:05:50,644 --> 00:05:54,878
Pytest, Vitest, Testing Library, Playwright, Ruff and Biome
verify the

99
00:05:54,898 --> 00:05:59,513
implementation. Locked dependencies make those environments
reproducible.

100
00:06:00,029 --> 00:06:02,889
There is no predictive AI model in the application.

101
00:06:04,347 --> 00:06:07,718
The service resolves the accepted release before using its
cache.

102
00:06:08,279 --> 00:06:12,406
Its context includes the release, parser, policies, applied
filters and

103
00:06:12,426 --> 00:06:16,598
build identifier. A canonical hash pins the analysis and
export.

104
00:06:17,133 --> 00:06:20,730
React checks the returned contract and displays values,
coverage and

105
00:06:20,750 --> 00:06:24,993
issue age. A stale export context is rejected instead of
returning a

106
00:06:25,013 --> 00:06:26,118
different analysis.

107
00:06:27,547 --> 00:06:31,018
The repository separates frontend views and typed clients from
Python

108
00:06:31,038 --> 00:06:34,361
API routes, services, domain logic and persistence.

109
00:06:34,893 --> 00:06:38,120
Migrations and operator ingestion have their own modules.

110
00:06:38,655 --> 00:06:42,151
Source fixtures, tests and verification scripts are explicit.

111
00:06:42,706 --> 00:06:46,607
The root README explains startup, the technology stack,
methodology,

112
00:06:46,680 --> 00:06:48,835
deployment evidence and AI assistance.

113
00:06:49,371 --> 00:06:52,404
Local secrets and generated output stay outside Git.

114
00:06:53,880 --> 00:06:57,410
In the decision service, the reader loads forecasts for the
pinned release

115
00:06:57,430 --> 00:06:59,441
and passes them to decision analysis.

116
00:06:59,963 --> 00:07:04,293
It never loads actuals here. The source selector and metric
functions

117
00:07:04,313 --> 00:07:08,967
are separate modules. Tests cover cutoff equality, invalid
latest keys,

118
00:07:09,087 --> 00:07:12,777
revised actuals, missing data and the January to February
boundary.

119
00:07:14,247 --> 00:07:18,664
This is deliberately a public, read-only dashboard, with no
user authentication

120
00:07:18,684 --> 00:07:23,325
flow. Protection relies on request validation, restrictive
browser headers,

121
00:07:23,368 --> 00:07:25,707
safe errors and a separate database reader.

122
00:07:26,262 --> 00:07:30,076
The reader cannot write, change schema, or access raw payload
bytes.

123
00:07:30,611 --> 00:07:33,230
Verified TLS protects the database connection.

124
00:07:33,775 --> 00:07:36,529
Operator credentials are absent from the web runtime.

125
00:07:37,980 --> 00:07:41,799
Caches have bounded size and lifetime, and concurrent requests
for one

126
00:07:41,819 --> 00:07:46,136
key share a calculation. Database pools and timeouts constrain
resource

127
00:07:46,156 --> 00:07:50,631
use. A local fifty-client test completed two hundred requests
at roughly

128
00:07:50,651 --> 00:07:54,186
four hundred and ninety-three milliseconds at the ninety-fifth
percentile,

129
00:07:54,239 --> 00:07:58,829
using a test-only quota. This is local API evidence, not a
hosted

130
00:07:58,849 --> 00:08:00,822
capacity or availability guarantee.

131
00:08:02,280 --> 00:08:05,376
The published continuous-integration run passed one hundred and
seven

132
00:08:05,396 --> 00:08:08,892
backend tests with no skips and forty-seven frontend tests.

133
00:08:09,415 --> 00:08:13,494
It also built Docker, replayed the real seed, exercised the
browser and

134
00:08:13,514 --> 00:08:18,322
exact downloads, restarted Postgres and web, and compared
unchanged fingerprints.

135
00:08:18,847 --> 00:08:22,734
The clean runner exposed database-reader isolation and
clipboard-permission

136
00:08:22,754 --> 00:08:26,023
test assumptions; both were corrected without changing the
production

137
00:08:26,043 --> 00:08:26,742
analysis.

138
00:08:28,180 --> 00:08:32,462
Vercel imports the root FastAPI application, builds React, and
bundles

139
00:08:32,482 --> 00:08:36,818
its compiled assets. The function region is configured as
London, with

140
00:08:36,838 --> 00:08:38,917
external Neon Postgres in London.

141
00:08:39,462 --> 00:08:41,367
The selected plans are free tiers.

142
00:08:41,912 --> 00:08:45,875
The function uses verified TLS, one pooled connection per
instance

143
00:08:45,895 --> 00:08:47,463
and a reader-role connection cap.

144
00:08:47,998 --> 00:08:50,935
Database initialization is a separate operator step.

145
00:08:52,380 --> 00:08:55,987
GitHub Actions verifies changes; it does not automatically
deploy this

146
00:08:56,007 --> 00:09:00,860
project. An authorized Vercel CLI deployment publishes a
reviewed revision.

147
00:09:01,415 --> 00:09:04,352
The deployment record identifies the source and dataset.

148
00:09:04,906 --> 00:09:08,725
Later documentation and test commits differ from the hosted
build, while

149
00:09:08,745 --> 00:09:11,913
a comparison verified eighty-nine identical runtime inputs.

150
00:09:12,449 --> 00:09:16,466
Replacing the hosted application preserved its accepted data
and results.

151
00:09:17,914 --> 00:09:21,510
Wind Desk connects a practical analyst workflow with explicit
temporal

152
00:09:21,530 --> 00:09:24,641
rules, durable source evidence and repeatable verification.

153
00:09:25,192 --> 00:09:29,397
Its next operational steps are agreed trading cutoffs,
scheduled receipt-aware

154
00:09:29,417 --> 00:09:33,830
data, distributed capacity controls, monitored recovery and
client acceptance.

155
00:09:34,365 --> 00:09:37,350
Explore the public application and repository shown here.

156
00:09:37,895 --> 00:09:39,424
Thank you for reviewing the project.

